{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "MosaicAstemMixedSurfaceEquilibrium",
    "authors": [
      "EqWeFiC"
    ],
    "description": "The PHYSICS of MOSAIC's gas-particle partitioning of HNO3, HCl and NH3 onto one MIXED size bin that holds solid NH4NO3 and/or NH4Cl beside a liquid: SUBROUTINE ASTEM_flux_mix with ASTEM_flux_mix_case4a / case4b (chem/module_mosaic_therm.F, WRF v4.8.0), which ASTEM_semi_volatiles calls for such a bin (any other mixed bin goes to ASTEM_flux_wet). It writes which equilibrium holds at the surface and the instantaneous rates kg (gas - surface) that follow; ASTEM's integrator (the explicit solid and semi-implicit liquid updates, the 1% equilibrium tests that switch a salt off -- signed for a liquid, FORTRAN_BUGS B31 -- and the step choice) is not here (CLAUDE.md: numerical solvers belong to EarthSciIntegrator).\n\nTHE CASES, as ASTEM_flux_mix tests them, from the bin's LIQUID sulfate ratio and its solid salts:\n  1. solid CaCO3, or 2. a sulfate-rich liquid (0 <= X_T < 1.9999): handed to the liquid surface (ASTEM_flux_wet_case1 / case2), so the rates are astem_liquid_surface_equilibrium.esm's (wet; never reached by a bin MOSAIC's phase state can produce in the hand scan, since conform_electrolytes leaves no CaCO3 beside a liquid and no NH4NO3 or NH4Cl beside a sulfate-rich one, but transcribed).\n  3. solid NaCl or CaCl2 with HNO3 in the gas: the solid surface's case 3 -- HNO3 displaces HCl one for one, and NH4Cl forms or evaporates at Keq_sg(2) (ASTEM_flux_dry_case3a/3b).\n  4. solid NH4NO3 and solid NH4Cl: the solid surface's case 4 (ASTEM_flux_dry_case4) at the pure solids' products.\n  4a. solid NH4NO3 only: the solid NH4NO3 surface (ASTEM_flux_dry_case4a at Keq_sg(1)) AND, beside it, the liquid's NH4Cl in solution equilibrium, s_NH3 s_HCl = keq_nh4cl = kel_NH3 kel_HCl a_NH4Cl kp_nh4cl with equal NH3 and HCl fluxes (ASTEM_flux_wet_case3b): two surfaces on one particle, each balancing NH3 against its own acid, and the bin takes both -- its NH3 rate is the sum. Nothing caps that sum at the diffusion limit kg_NH3 g_NH3 (each surface's own NH3 flux is capped, their sum is not; ASTEM_flux_dry_case4ab does scale two solid salts together): FORTRAN_BUGS B32, reproduced here so the rates are the Fortran's.\n  4b. solid NH4Cl only: the solid NH4Cl surface and the liquid's NH4NO3 (ASTEM_flux_wet_case3a), likewise.\nA single-salt surface's NH3 is the larger root of kg_NH3 s^2 + (kg_acid g_acid - kg_NH3 g_NH3) s - kg_acid K = 0 (FUNCTION quadratic, template mosaic_quadratic) -- the same balance the solid surface solves, with the solution's product K in place of the solid's. ASTEM_flux_mix's cases 5 and 6 (no solid NH4NO3 or NH4Cl) cannot be reached from ASTEM_semi_volatiles, which calls it only when one is present; the rates are 0 there.\n\nWHAT IS MOUNTED AROUND IT. The solid pieces are astem_solid_surface_equilibrium.esm's (acid_hno3, f3b, f4a, f4b, scale4, nh3_need) evaluated with mixed = 1, because ASTEM_flux_mix resets Keq_nh4no3_0 = Keq_sg(1), Keq_nh4cl_0 = Keq_sg(2) where ASTEM_flux_dry uses min(Kp0, Keq_sg); the solution products keq_nh4no3 / keq_nh4cl and the case 1/2 rates are astem_liquid_surface_equilibrium.esm's. The coupling documents lift all three pointwise over lev x bin (couplings/mosaic_astem_rates.esm, couplings/mosaic_column.esm) and astem_rate_assembly.esm takes this component's rates for its route_mix bins.\n\nNOT TRANSCRIBED (state edits, which the tests feed the state AFTER): absorb_tiny_nh4cl/nh4no3 and degas_tiny_nh4cl/nh4no3 before case 4a/4b (they move 1% of a gas or of the electrolytes into or out of the solution so that the salt's activity is defined), degas_solid_nh4no3/nh4cl (an undersaturated salt below ptol_mol_astem evaporated at once). Nor the H+ molality ASTEM_flux_mix re-diagnoses from the surface HNO3 or HCl: it feeds no rate.\n\nReference: hand-specified mixed bins run through WRF's own compiled ASTEM (kernels/mosaic_therm_driver mode 6; chem170_scm/mosaic_astem/make_astem_mix_hand.py -> mix.tape; data/eqwefic/notes/chem170_mosaic_astem_capture.md), real(kind=8), rel 1e-9. The chem_opt = 170 column never reaches ASTEM_flux_mix.",
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Zaveri, R.A., Easter, R.C., Fast, J.D., Peters, L.K. (2008). MOSAIC. J. Geophys. Res. 113, D13204."
      },
      {
        "citation": "WRF v4.8.0 chem/module_mosaic_therm.F, ASTEM_flux_mix, ASTEM_flux_mix_case4a/4b, ASTEM_flux_wet_case3a/3b, FUNCTION quadratic"
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "MosaicAstemMixedSurfaceEquilibrium": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "./mosaic_thermo_templates.esm"
        }
      ],
